Z||000008||Huck||02-22-2001||08:11 PM||||I understand where your comming from.  My GT is all I have to drive in the winter too, but I avoid it as much as possible.  I live in a small town and can walk everywhere I need to go.  If I have to go out of town when its bad out, I'll take my truck, but it doesn't have valid plates or insurance, and itsnt a whole lot better in the snow than the fiero.  Bald tires are a ***** .  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I cant wait till spring to actually drive my baby everyday.  Some a$$hole keyed the crap out of my car and truck on a random spree there in November, then a friend put his trailer hitch through my front end.  So my baby's gonna have a new front clip and fresh paint all the way around by the middle of april... now if only those T-tops would stop leaking...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Mark<BR>86 2m4<BR>87 GT T-top||||reg||1
